1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,410
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,910
I'm only waiting
exactly five minutes.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:16,590
I can finally breathe.
Why is it so hot today?

5
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,690
I'm sorry I'm late. Let's go.

6
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:20,960
Get up, hurry.

7
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:22,760
Aren't you being
a little too shameless?

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,530
About what? Me?

9
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,670
I just apologized to you.

10
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:30,170
Then why did you snatch my water?

11
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,340
This?

12
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:43,010
Hey, I thought our country was known
for being generous with water.

13
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:44,950
I'm sorry again.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,490
- I will buy you a new one.
- Forget it.

15
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:50,720
What's wrong?

16
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,460
Hold on a second.

17
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:03,200
Why are you laughing?
Just wait. This really helps.

18
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,570
First, take my hand and stand up.

19
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:11,680
Can you stand?

20
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:16,510
Then listen to me
and take three steps back.

21
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:18,380
- One.
- One.

22
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,450
- Two.
- Two.

23
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,420
Good job. Now, one step forward.

24
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,920
- One.
- One.

25
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,420
- Two.
- Two.

26
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:40,840
Mom, at this rate,
my face is going to explode.

27
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:43,610
How is it?

28
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,580
It's going to explode.

29
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:48,310
What is?

30
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:53,250
It felt like the veins in my calves
were going to explode.

31
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,620
I can walk now.

32
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:57,990
Where did you learn this?

33
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,390
It's really effective.

34
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:05,500
I learned it from my girlfriend.

35
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:08,030
I see.

36
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,130
Let's go.

37
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,140
It's not that way. It's this way.

38
00:02:15,610 --> 00:02:17,240
Why are you acting like
you know the way?

39
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,210
Stay close and follow me.

40
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:24,450
Don't follow too closely, though.
Maybe about this much?

41
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:26,250
Keep this much distance.

42
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:32,120
I have no intention of sticking
right next to you either.

43
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,400
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

44
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,310
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

45
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,540
I have to pay for
our Da Mi's wedding.

46
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:54,310
I saved this money
to marry off my daughter.

47
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,350
Don't take another step.

48
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:03,620
Can't you see I'm in a bad mood?

49
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:08,030
No. I wasn't trying to go near you.

50
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:12,630
She definitely has eyes
on the top of her head.

51
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:23,070
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

52
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,640
What?

53
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:28,750
Where do you want me
to deliver this, Director?

54
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:32,050
You want me to deliver this...

55
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,390
to Mi Mi's Chicken Soup?

56
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:37,860
Yes. I've already visited
all the other stores...

57
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:38,890
and said my greetings.

58
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:40,790
I have a lot of other things to do.

59
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:42,630
Please hurry and go.

60
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:45,360
Okay.

61
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,300
What are you doing?

62
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:50,070
Please get going.
I'm counting on you.

63
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,600
Yes, sir.

64
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:55,410
(Deokjin Rice Cake Shop)

65
00:03:57,110 --> 00:04:01,380
- My stomach! I'm dying.
- Goodness.

66
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:04,750
Park Ji Young, what's wrong?
Does your stomach hurt?

67
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:09,150
Yes, Director.
I suddenly have a stomachache...

68
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:10,790
Let's go
to the examination room first.

69
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:11,990
I'll take a look.

70
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:15,060
- It could be appendicitis.
- No.

71
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,900
I need to go to the restroom first.

72
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:21,230
Really? Then hurry up and go.

73
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,570
Yes, Director. By the way...

74
00:04:24,570 --> 00:04:26,700
I'm sorry, but could you hand out
the rice cakes for me?

75
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:29,870
Yes, don't worry about that.

76
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:52,200
Hold it in.

77
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:56,400
You can keep wondering.
It won't kill you, so don't worry.

78
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:57,970
Yes.

79
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:04,410
Goodness. Who might this be?

80
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:06,240
How have you been, ma'am?

81
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:10,350
Yes. Congratulations on opening.

82
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,850
I didn't recognize you as a doctor.

83
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,690
Welcome, Doctor.

84
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:17,020
How did the opening go?

85
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:19,520
Are there any problems
inside the shop?

86
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:21,030
None at all.

87
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,160
I heard
from the real estate agent...

88
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,700
that it was vacant
for quite a while,

89
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:28,370
but it seems you've maintained it
very cleanly in the meantime.

90
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:29,830
Yes.

91
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:33,870
Our President Jo is very diligent.

92
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:39,580
Since you do precious work
of healing and saving sick people,

93
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:43,180
always take good care
of your own body and mind,

94
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,680
and may you prosper.

95
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,250
Yes, ma'am, thank you.

96
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:50,890
And these are rice cakes
to celebrate the opening.

97
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:54,360
Goodness. It's rare for shops
to hand out rice cakes...

98
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,260
like this these days, Doctor.

99
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,900
Is your nose stuffed?
Do you have a cold?

100
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:04,000
No, why?

101
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,240
Never mind.

102
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:09,840
Thank you for thinking
of us, Doctor.

103
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:13,980
Don't think of us
as just your landlord.

104
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:17,750
Think of us as neighbors
making a living in the same alley,

105
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,890
and let's help each other out
if there's anything we can do.

106
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:23,790
Yes. Just hearing you say that
is reassuring, President Jo.

107
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,360
I look forward to working with you.

108
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:31,330
Doctor, have you had lunch
by any chance?

109
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:35,600
You must have walked a lot
handing out the rice cakes,

110
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:39,100
so how about I make you
some ginseng chicken soup?

111
00:06:40,610 --> 00:06:41,770
I've had lunch.

112
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,640
I'll stop by with my staff
next time.

113
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:45,310
I'll be going now.

114
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,550
Yes. Goodbye.

115
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:51,680
Please make sure to come.
And stop by every day if you can.

116
00:06:53,790 --> 00:06:55,090
Oh, my.

117
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:59,490
That whining sound you make
whenever you see a handsome man...

118
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:00,730
never seems to get old.

119
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:04,560
Just you wait, Mrs. Choi.

120
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:08,170
- Wait for what?
- Someday,

121
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:12,000
I'm definitely going to make
that man mine.

122
00:07:14,610 --> 00:07:15,610
Why you...

123
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:17,510
Do you have no filter
in front of Mother?

124
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,140
You have been burned enough by men.

125
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:22,310
And do you have no shame?

126
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:25,050
You really need to act your age.

127
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,090
Don't be too hard on her, Mi Mi.

128
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:33,290
Even though people age year by year,
it's only the body that gets old.

129
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:36,230
The mind stays exactly the same
for everyone.

130
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,860
How mature do you think you are?

131
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,500
Right, Mrs. Choi?

132
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,840
Seriously, Mi Mi, I'm a grown woman.

133
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,570
Why did you smack
the back of my head?

134
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:49,440
We are both getting older together.

135
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:53,740
Your only sister just wants to date
and maybe get married.

136
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:56,850
I want to have a husband listed
on my family register too.

137
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:00,750
Ri Ja, your courage is commendable,

138
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:03,190
but watch your words and actions.

139
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,220
What did I do?

140
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:08,330
In today's world,
if you are not careful,

141
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:12,130
before you even seduce him,
you will end up in handcuffs.

142
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:16,330
- Mrs. Choi.
- Listen to her, Ri Ja.

143
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,700
If you go to jail this time,
I will not bail you out.

144
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:31,420
I came home to rest for a bit,
but you haven't even unpacked.

145
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,680
Where are you roaming around?

146
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,720
The thing is, Hak Sung,

147
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:38,320
- I got a job.
- You did what?

148
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,960
I said I got a job.

149
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,830
You really did?

150
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:46,930
But why are you
whispering like that?

151
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:50,300
I think I got a job
where I shouldn't have.

152
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,370
What do you mean,
where you shouldn't have?

153
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,040
Where is it?

154
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:58,280
Don't tell me you took a job
at some shady place...

155
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,110
just because they offered
a lot of money.

156
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:03,410
Oh, they are coming.

157
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:04,980
Talk to you at home. I'm hanging up.

158
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:12,090
She is blinded by money.

159
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:17,500
Surely she hasn't
lost her mind that badly.

160
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:22,600
But where on earth
did she get a job?

161
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:26,700
(Songi Kindergarten)

162
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,710
- Eun A's mom.
- Hello.

163
00:09:28,770 --> 00:09:30,940
- It has been a while.
- How have you been?

164
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:32,240
- The beach was so nice.
- Goodness.

165
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,180
But is that Su Ah's dad over there?

166
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:37,580
- Yes, I think so.
- You know, lately,

167
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:39,550
Su Ah's dad has been the one
dropping her off.

168
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,190
(Factory Production Line
Worker Recruitment)

169
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:49,490
Hello, applicant.
Thank you for your interest...

170
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,900
and for taking the time and effort
to apply to our company.

171
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,560
We sincerely appreciate it.

172
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:57,130
After careful consideration,
we regret to inform you...

173
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,700
that we will not be moving forward
with your application at this time.

174
00:10:02,910 --> 00:10:05,340
If I need to pay 600 dollars
for living expenses right away,

175
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:07,710
I have to do something.

176
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:11,380
Do I have to get a part-time job
at a distribution center?

177
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,350
Or maybe...

178
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:15,450
a night shift
at a convenience store?

179
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:20,360
Deliveries...
Apartments are tough, though.

180
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:23,590
Food delivery?
I don't have a motorcycle.

181
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:28,030
What are you thinking about?

182
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,970
You should take
whatever you can get.

183
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,640
What do you want?

184
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,940
Are you at an ice cream shop
right now?

185
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,010
Picking out flavors?

186
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:37,640
Are you really in a position...

187
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,980
to be picking and choosing
right now?

188
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:44,280
Excuse me, who are you?

189
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:47,350
Who are you to just start
talking down to me?

190
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:50,760
I have never seen
a woman like you before.

191
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:53,560
You have a way to make money
right in front of you,

192
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,190
so why are you wasting time
thinking of other things?

193
00:10:56,430 --> 00:10:58,660
What are you talking about now?

194
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,260
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.

195
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:01,830
What?

196
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,040
Grandma's knees
have been bad for years.

197
00:11:05,170 --> 00:11:06,600
If I were Su Ah's dad,

198
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:09,270
I would learn the kitchen work
from the crack of dawn.

199
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:11,840
She would at least
cover your living expenses.

200
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:14,080
And Mother would probably
give you and Su Ah...

201
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,650
enough allowance for what you need.

202
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:18,520
If you showed her that you were...

203
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:21,250
working your tail off
for 12 hours a day, that is.

204
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:24,390
Hey, I still used to...

205
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:27,930
run a proper business
under my own name.

206
00:11:28,290 --> 00:11:32,300
Are you telling Kang Gang Nam
to go boil chicken soup?

207
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,870
Just chicken soup?

208
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:39,870
You still haven't come
to your senses, have you?

209
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,840
Go ahead and do whatever you want.

210
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:45,610
Hey, where are you going?

211
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:47,010
Hey, Su Ah...

212
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:50,880
Are you leaving
without seeing Su Ah?

213
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,420
I have to go to work.
I'm on the afternoon shift.

214
00:11:56,820 --> 00:12:00,760
I'm so pathetic.
I guess I'm pathetic enough...

215
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:03,090
to come all the way here
after our divorce...

216
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,930
just to stand here
and worry about you.

217
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:09,030
This is really the end.
Good luck doing it all on your own.

218
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,600
Hey, if you are making money,

219
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:14,640
shouldn't you at least
pay child support?

220
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:19,040
I'm the one raising her, after all.
Mi Seon. Kim Mi Seon!

221
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,180
Honey!

222
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,950
Child support? Crazy jerk.

223
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:26,150
After all the business debts
I paid off for him.

224
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:28,420
See if I ever send him
a single dollar.

225
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:34,760
Su Ah.

226
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,390
I'm sorry.

227
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:38,960
Seriously...

228
00:12:43,130 --> 00:12:44,270
Goodness...

229
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:45,940
I'm sorry, Madam.

230
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,540
Please, let me get it for you.

231
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:51,080
If I can't even get my own water,

232
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:53,180
it is time for me
to leave this world.

233
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:56,480
But what are you writing
so diligently?

234
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:58,850
I'm making a grocery list
for the memorial service.

235
00:12:58,850 --> 00:12:59,880
I see.

236
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:02,250
I need to write it down in advance
so I buy fewer unnecessary things...

237
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,050
and save money.

238
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:07,660
If I don't write it down like this,
it feels like I'm being robbed.

239
00:13:08,230 --> 00:13:10,590
The market prices are scary
these days, Madam.

240
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:13,530
Come a little closer.

241
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,700
I have something I need you to do.

242
00:13:17,770 --> 00:13:18,840
- Yes.
- Yes.

243
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:21,870
Well.

244
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:26,410
Do Yun's mother won't prepare
for the memorial service...

245
00:13:26,810 --> 00:13:28,050
with her own hands.

246
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,020
So, Mrs. Anseong,

247
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,220
just do as I tell you...

248
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,220
Right.

249
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:38,260
Yes.

250
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:40,060
Yes, Madam.

251
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,590
- Yes.
- Okay.

252
00:13:44,230 --> 00:13:45,230
Good.

253
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,030
Please do that.

254
00:13:48,730 --> 00:13:51,240
- Hey. Now, let's go.
- Now, let's go and see.

255
00:13:56,510 --> 00:13:58,080
- Goodness.
- Give me a break.

256
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:01,180
- Just fall off the board.
- All right.

257
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:02,280
Fall.

258
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:09,890
Now, me.

259
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:14,290
Here we go.

260
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,390
No way.

261
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:18,430
- It's a gae.
- Goodness.

262
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,360
- It's a gae.
- That's it, right, now.

263
00:14:20,430 --> 00:14:22,100
Well, it looks like...

264
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,670
I'll be getting a free bowl
of blood sausage soup today.

265
00:14:23,930 --> 00:14:27,910
Taking the Cheonan subway line
all the way here was worth it.

266
00:14:27,910 --> 00:14:28,970
Hey.

267
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:33,180
That's not it.
If they get a geol over there,

268
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,580
that bottom piece will get caught.

269
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:37,980
Gosh. You're right.

270
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:41,090
Thank you, young man.

271
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,860
Hey, young man.

272
00:14:44,990 --> 00:14:47,420
Why are you out here
in the middle of the day...

273
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,560
on a weekday?

274
00:14:49,990 --> 00:14:51,000
Excuse me?

275
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:54,700
Why is a perfectly healthy young man
killing time around here?

276
00:14:55,030 --> 00:14:56,830
You are at the prime age
to be working.

277
00:14:57,200 --> 00:15:00,900
Hurry up and leave.
This place belongs to us.

278
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:05,710
No, I was just trying
to look around the park.

279
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:09,680
And it's not like this place
belongs entirely to seniors, right?

280
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:12,550
Stop giving advice and just go.

281
00:15:26,930 --> 00:15:27,930
Goodness.

282
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,140
Now, is it my turn?

283
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:35,240
Now, I just need to catch them again,
of course.

284
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:37,980
- All right, let's go.
- Let's go!

285
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:40,010
Now, watch this.

286
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,280
It's a mo!

287
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:45,820
- It's a mo.
- A mo!.

288
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,720
- It's a mo!
- Who is this?

289
00:15:47,790 --> 00:15:49,520
Now, what do we need to get?

290
00:15:54,590 --> 00:15:56,190
The customer you are calling
is unavailable.

291
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:57,390
Please leave a message
after the tone...

292
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,200
You're really not going to answer,
Kang Dae Chi?

293
00:16:02,470 --> 00:16:04,840
Did you think I would give up easily
just because of this?

294
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,840
Cha Se Na is coming for you.

295
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,510
Just you wait.

296
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:17,250
My handsome number one debtor.

297
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:19,420
Yes.

298
00:16:21,090 --> 00:16:24,420
So, Do Yun,
you need to help Seung Yun a lot.

299
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,490
Since he has lived
in the States all this time,

300
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,130
adjusting to
the company culture here...

301
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:29,330
might be difficult for him.

302
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,930
I have already instructed
the staff about that,

303
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,760
so you do not have to worry, honey.

304
00:16:34,730 --> 00:16:36,470
A busy person like you,
thinking of Seung Yun...

305
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:38,600
and spending
your entire afternoon here.

306
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,040
Do you really not need
to go back to the office?

307
00:16:41,610 --> 00:16:43,270
I will just leave when you leave.

308
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,210
You said you are going to a meeting
with Summit Investment.

309
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:46,980
Do Yun, are you not going?

310
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:49,580
Assistant Manager Kang will escort
her instead of me.

311
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:53,080
I'm busy with the proposal
for the first half of next year.

312
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:54,750
- Yes.
- Like the executives and staff,

313
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:57,760
I have high expectations of you too,
Team Leader Cha Do Yun.

314
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,330
I will do my best
to meet them, ma'am.

315
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,160
Good.

316
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:09,170
Do Yun, my meeting today
is a really important one.

317
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,470
Things really need to go well.

318
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,300
Will you cheer for me?

319
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:16,870
Even without my cheering,
you will do perfectly fine.

320
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,680
Do I look like
such a capable person...

321
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,080
in my son's eyes?

322
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:23,710
I'm honored.

323
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,380
Now, we should get going.

324
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:28,550
You said you need to stop by
the department store first.

325
00:17:28,690 --> 00:17:29,790
All right, let's go.

326
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,900
(Wholesale Dishware Market)

327
00:17:46,870 --> 00:17:48,510
(1 for 5 dollars, 2 for 8 dollars)

328
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,810
(Flower)

329
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,400
It's pretty.

330
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:17,970
Excuse me.

331
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,340
We have to go.

332
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:25,740
Why? I was right
in the middle of looking.

333
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,310
Kang Da Mi,

334
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,910
why do you think I asked you
to come here with me?

335
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:31,850
Well, obviously,

336
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:34,320
you wanted to show me
where to find cheap things.

337
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:36,790
"Obviously."

338
00:18:38,290 --> 00:18:39,290
Or...

339
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:42,130
maybe you wanted to show me
a place with a variety of clothes?

340
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:46,100
You've blown all those contests
or internship opportunities...

341
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,430
so far, right?

342
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:50,230
I think I know the reason why.

343
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:53,400
What did you say?
Are you done talking now?

344
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:57,670
I just said it out of frustration,
but I guess it was true.

345
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:01,710
I'm the one who is frustrated.
Tell me.

346
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:03,910
Don't just look at me in a way
that makes me feel bad.

347
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,550
Why are you only looking
at clothes...

348
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,190
when you want to make them?

349
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:15,590
Then what should I look at?

350
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:18,530
What else should I look at?

351
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:19,960
I'm at a clothing store,
so I look at clothes.

352
00:19:20,230 --> 00:19:21,870
- It's nice here.
- Why did we come here?

353
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:22,900
Why? It's nice here.

354
00:19:22,970 --> 00:19:25,200
- Hey, what is that?
- That's totally my style!

355
00:19:26,270 --> 00:19:27,970
I called dibs on this.

356
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:29,670
- Come on.
- Hey, it looks good on you.

357
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,390
Wait...

358
00:19:51,430 --> 00:19:52,660
Why are you laughing?

359
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:56,400
Do you know you have a knack
for subtly offending people?

360
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:59,140
I'm sorry.
The situation was just a bit funny.

361
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:02,910
Get up.

362
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:12,020
What are you doing? Come on.

363
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:19,490
Tell me. You have to tell me.

364
00:20:19,890 --> 00:20:20,920
Tell you what?

365
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,960
You asked me
why I only looked at clothes.

366
00:20:23,090 --> 00:20:25,960
You asked why I only look at clothes
when I want to make clothes.

367
00:20:33,970 --> 00:20:37,040
Why do you want to become
a fashion designer, Kang Da Mi?

368
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,810
Because I want to see
many people wearing...

369
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:44,350
the clothes that I designed
and created.

370
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,350
Right, many people.

371
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,750
Then you shouldn't
look at the clothes first.

372
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:52,420
You should look at the people first.
And you must always, every day,

373
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:54,520
make those people
your top priority...

374
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:57,030
and observe them very carefully.

375
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:59,700
The consumers who will wear
the clothes you make...

376
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:01,870
are not robots.
They are human beings.

377
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:03,700
Do you understand a little bit?

378
00:21:05,270 --> 00:21:09,110
Your designs, Kang Da Mi,
only have ideas about the clothes,

379
00:21:09,170 --> 00:21:11,010
but they lack an understanding...

380
00:21:11,070 --> 00:21:12,480
of the people
who will actually wear them.

381
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,520
Wait for me.

382
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:37,030
Welcome, ma'am. How have you been?

383
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:39,870
I have prepared the shoes
you requested to be repaired.

384
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:46,180
It's a pleasure to meet you.

385
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:48,050
I'm Song Min Hee.
A staff member here.

386
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:51,780
So you are a staff member.

387
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:57,690
Ma'am, would you like
to try on the shoes?

388
00:21:57,990 --> 00:21:59,520
I don't see Manager Kang.

389
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:01,590
Manager Kang...

390
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:04,060
took today off for personal reasons.

391
00:22:05,530 --> 00:22:07,030
She took the day off?

392
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:11,000
Even though she knew perfectly well
that I was visiting the store today.

393
00:22:12,670 --> 00:22:13,670
Well...

394
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:16,910
- That is enough.
- Pardon?

395
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:18,880
What are you doing?
Put the shoes down.

396
00:22:19,510 --> 00:22:20,540
Yes, ma'am.

397
00:22:38,030 --> 00:22:40,160
You reduced the heels
by exactly three centimeters, right?

398
00:22:40,430 --> 00:22:41,500
Of course, ma'am.

399
00:22:41,670 --> 00:22:44,330
They were reduced by exactly
three centimeters without any error.

400
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,740
Throw away the ones I wore here.

401
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:51,010
- Let's go, Assistant Manager Kang.
- Yes, ma'am.

402
00:22:55,050 --> 00:22:57,980
(K Department Store)

403
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,190
Breathe.

404
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:06,820
Breathe.

405
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:13,960
Those are 2,400 dollars.

406
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:17,070
Your price tag is
my actual monthly salary.

407
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:21,240
The world is truly unfair.

408
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:24,740
Right?

409
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:26,680
Yes?

410
00:23:45,830 --> 00:23:47,830
(Business Hours: 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.)

411
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:19,930
What are you looking at?

412
00:24:21,870 --> 00:24:23,970
Hey. That's a mini car, right?

413
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:30,440
There must be quite a few people
who collect really old toys,

414
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:32,010
seeing how they sell them like this.

415
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,150
What's the point of teaching you?

416
00:24:35,210 --> 00:24:37,110
You forget it
in less than 30 minutes.

417
00:24:38,010 --> 00:24:39,650
When I came in, I already scanned...

418
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:40,920
all the customers in here
at a glance.

419
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:42,350
From people in their 20s
to their 40s.

420
00:24:42,650 --> 00:24:45,290
And those in their 40s are mostly
male customers.

421
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,260
Do you think I'm an idiot?

422
00:24:48,490 --> 00:24:49,990
Well, then I will ask you
one more question.

423
00:24:50,230 --> 00:24:53,800
Kang Da Mi, why do you think people
come to visit this place?

424
00:24:57,370 --> 00:24:58,570
That's because...

425
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:01,870
If I say
it's because it's cheap again,

426
00:25:01,940 --> 00:25:03,670
he will immediately say I'm wrong
and turn around, right?

427
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:05,940
What is it?

428
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:09,210
Why do they come
to a place like this?

429
00:25:16,390 --> 00:25:17,490
Are you giving up this time too?

430
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:20,360
Who said I'm giving up?
I know the answer now.

431
00:25:21,190 --> 00:25:24,230
People come to a place
like this because...

432
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:31,100
They come to find props
or clothes...

433
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:33,500
that show their identity.

434
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:35,110
Their own individuality,

435
00:25:35,540 --> 00:25:37,840
a sort of identity, you could say.

436
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:45,480
Excuse me.

437
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:50,120
Please wrap this mini car,
that track over there,

438
00:25:50,190 --> 00:25:52,120
and this teddy bear.

439
00:25:52,190 --> 00:25:54,220
Thank you, sir.

440
00:25:55,130 --> 00:25:56,490
How would you like to pay?

441
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:58,900
By credit card, please.

442
00:25:59,930 --> 00:26:02,530
Okay, please wait a moment.
I will wrap them up right away.

443
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:04,300
Okay.

444
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:25,960
Seung Yun, how can this
run all by itself?

445
00:26:26,260 --> 00:26:27,820
It's so fascinating,
and I'm curious.

446
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:29,860
Do Yun, this mini car...

447
00:26:29,890 --> 00:26:31,290
has something called a motor
attached to it.

448
00:26:32,130 --> 00:26:35,230
To make it run fast
and turn corners well,

449
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:38,300
Dad even bought a gold motor
and a black motor for us yesterday.

450
00:26:38,300 --> 00:26:39,800
So I swapped them out.

451
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,340
This time, you try it yourself,
Do Yun.

452
00:26:42,410 --> 00:26:45,410
You have to be able to do everything
yourself with your own strength.

453
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:46,640
Got it?

454
00:26:46,710 --> 00:26:49,350
Yes, you are really smart,
Seung Yun.

455
00:26:49,410 --> 00:26:50,610
You are the best.

456
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:54,180
- Kid, go ahead and try it. Here.
- Okay.

457
00:26:55,050 --> 00:26:56,050
Turn this side on.

458
00:26:57,150 --> 00:27:00,160
Now, let's try it. One, two, three.

459
00:27:02,630 --> 00:27:05,100
- It's really fast.
- You are right. It's super fast.

460
00:27:07,530 --> 00:27:09,770
Have a good day, sir.
I will come back next time.

461
00:27:10,870 --> 00:27:13,240
But hey, why are you
not saying anything?

462
00:27:13,870 --> 00:27:15,310
I answered your question.

463
00:27:15,610 --> 00:27:18,170
You have to tell me
if I'm right or if I'm wrong.

464
00:27:19,010 --> 00:27:20,180
Am I wrong again?

465
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:22,150
Here.

466
00:27:22,510 --> 00:27:24,010
Isn't this the teddy bear
from earlier?

467
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,150
Why are you giving this to me?

468
00:27:25,980 --> 00:27:26,980
It's a prize.

469
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:29,720
- What?
- It's a prize.

470
00:27:30,050 --> 00:27:31,920
Because you understood
what I taught you,

471
00:27:32,020 --> 00:27:33,760
and you answered
my question correctly.

472
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:35,730
Let's get going.

473
00:27:35,790 --> 00:27:37,260
Walking around for a while
made me hungry.

474
00:27:40,330 --> 00:27:41,330
I got it right.

475
00:27:43,070 --> 00:27:45,100
But he could've bought me a new one.

476
00:27:45,870 --> 00:27:47,870
Isn't this just cute trash?

477
00:27:49,810 --> 00:27:50,940
You're hungry?

478
00:27:52,180 --> 00:27:53,980
How about tteokbokki, fritters,
and sundae for dinner?

479
00:27:54,580 --> 00:27:55,680
It's on me today.

480
00:27:56,110 --> 00:27:58,310
I'm not usually the type
to treat people,

481
00:27:58,380 --> 00:27:59,680
but I learned
something special today.

482
00:28:00,650 --> 00:28:01,650
Hello?

483
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:04,350
(Mission: Mompossible)

484
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:06,160
You're so mean, Mom.

485
00:28:06,390 --> 00:28:07,690
If you want to eat it, just buy it.

486
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:09,290
Why are you just standing there
staring at it?

487
00:28:09,830 --> 00:28:11,490
No, it's not that I want to eat it.

488
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,860
It just reminded me of something.

489
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:15,500
Do you happen to like chicken soup?

490
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:17,170
There's a place called
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup...

491
00:28:19,040 --> 00:28:20,070
Who was that?

492
00:28:20,670 --> 00:28:22,610
That's definitely Hak Sung.

493
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:26,180
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
